  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1229 AM CST Mon Nov 2 2026\n\nThe cold front mentioned previously should be well southeast of our \narea by Tuesday evening leaving with it a much drier airmass and \nsomewhat windy conditions. We are not however expecting nearly as \nstrong of winds as we had during our last front. Wednesday and \nbeyond we should experience much more pleasant weather with highs in \nthe 70s, and lows in the 40s and 50s. Though the biggest change will \nbe the humidity as we will go from seeing dewpoints in the 60s and \nlow 70s prior to the arrival of the front to seeing 50s and some \nupper 40s after the front. This will certainly help things to feel \nmore seasonable and fall like compared to our recent stretch of \nsummer-like weather. Global models are hinting at another front \nmoving over our area over the weekend but consistency and timing \nissues remain. For now enjoy the beautiful fall like weather for \nthis upcoming week.",
